# Milestone: M3
# Covers: loader rejects v1.1 (M2) bytecode modules at v1.2 runtime
#
# deferred: v1.x — a host-driver verb that loads raw chunk bytes, without which an old version byte cannot reach the loader.
# matrix-row: wire-format
#
# Reason: the chk runner (tests/integration/run_chk.sh) feeds .u source text
# into the REPL.  There is no mechanism to inject a pre-baked binary blob and
# call uchunk_deserialize directly.
#
# NO C-LEVEL COVERAGE of an old-version rejection today.  The two unit
# cases that used to pin it went with the old loader's test file.  What
# stands is tests/rt/test_api.c::compile_then_load, which round-trips a
# real chunk through urbi_compile / urbi_load and asserts that eight bytes
# of garbage are refused -- that is the BAD_MAGIC arm, not the
# UNSUPPORTED_VERSION one this fixture is about.
#
# To activate, the runner needs binary-blob injection:
#   1. Hand-craft a blob with version byte 0x11 at offset 4.
#   2. Load it through a host-driver directive and assert the diagnostic
#      names the unsupported version.
